    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n59545" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόχλος</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>shell-fish with a spiral
			shell</i>, used for dyeing purple, Lat. <i>murex</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				528a1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				5.227
			</span></i> (Paul. Sil.); used as a trumpet, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IT</u>
				303
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				22.75
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Mosch.
				2.124
			</span></i>: also fem., <i><span class="en">
				Naumach.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Stob.
				4.31.76
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				3.21.6
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κασπίῃ ἐν κ.</span>, of a
			large sea-shell, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				3.859
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>land snail</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mir.</u>
				846b13
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>kohl</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				728.47
			</span></i>.</div>
